                          "text":  "I always knew I would not last. In the far north the Sun sinks lower every day in autumn, and I run on sunlight. Dust storms made it worse. On November 2, 2008, I sent my last signal.\n\nThen winter came and buried me in dry-ice frost. Pictures taken from orbit later showed my solar panels had been damaged, probably by the weight of that ice. I had five months. I found what I was sent to find.",
